From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Fix gallery not opening from the capture thumbnail
 (camera freeze)

Bug: tapping the capture thumbnail after taking a photo/video did not
open the Gallery and left the camera preview stuck/unresponsive.

Root cause: patch 0007 ("Change com.android.camera.action.REVIEW to
android.provider.action.REVIEW") changed the outgoing "review" intent
built in the thumbnail-tap handler (GalleryHelper.gotoGallery, called
from the thumbnail click path) to use the action
"android.provider.action.REVIEW" with no package/category set. Our
MIUIGalleryGlobal.apk (com.miui.gallery, the HyperOS Gallery port used
on this device) does not declare any <intent-filter> for that action.
So startActivity() throws ActivityNotFoundException.

That exception IS caught, but the fallback handler
(GalleryHelper.s(), "review activity not found!") retries with an
explicit setPackage("com.miui.mediaviewer") -- a separate MIUI system
component not part of this device's proprietary blobs -- so the
fallback ALSO throws ActivityNotFoundException, silently swallowed.
Since gotoGallery() already calls Camera.Co()/pauses the preview
before either startActivity() attempt, both failures being swallowed
is what makes the camera appear stuck/frozen instead of opening the
gallery or erroring visibly.

Fix: point the thumbnail-review intent at
"com.android.camera.action.REVIEW", which MIUIGalleryGlobal does
declare (see ExternalPhotoPageActivity in its manifest, alongside
android.intent.action.VIEW). This was already the action in use
before patch 0007 changed it, so it is the best-tested option in this
patch chain.

Note: an earlier version of this fix used
"com.miui.camera.action.REVIEW" instead, which the Gallery also
declares -- but that one routes to
TranslucentExternalPhotoPageActivity, MIUI's "seamless" camera->gallery
transition activity. That activity reads the "device_orientation"
extra MiuiCamera sends (see GalleryHelper.i()) to line up its
transition animation with the sensor orientation at capture time; on
this Gallery build that produced an extra 180 degree rotation on the
opened photo/video. ExternalPhotoPageActivity (reached via
"com.android.camera.action.REVIEW") does not do that
transition-matching, it just honors the image's EXIF orientation, so
it does not hit this rotation bug.

This mirrors the change into camera version 5.3.001050.2's current
(re-obfuscated) class names: what shipped as l3.smali/a6.smali in
older MiuiCamera builds is now r3.smali/o6.smali in the currently
vendored APK, so this patch targets those files instead of
l3.smali/a6.smali directly.

This does not touch patch 0006's "Support third party galleries"
change (the separate general "open Gallery app" intent, matched via
category android.intent.category.APP_GALLERY on the main launcher
activity), which already resolves correctly and is unaffected by this
bug.
---
 smali/com/android/camera/o6.smali | 2 +-
 smali/com/android/camera/r3.smali | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/smali/com/android/camera/o6.smali b/smali/com/android/camera/o6.smali
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/smali/com/android/camera/o6.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/camera/o6.smali
@@ -210,7 +210,7 @@

 .field public static final d1:Ljava/lang/String; = "com.miui.securitycenter.action.INVISIBLE_SETTING"

-.field public static final e:Ljava/lang/String; = "android.provider.action.REVIEW"
+.field public static final e:Ljava/lang/String; = "com.android.camera.action.REVIEW"

 .field public static final e0:I = 0x8c36

diff --git a/smali/com/android/camera/r3.smali b/smali/com/android/camera/r3.smali
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/smali/com/android/camera/r3.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/camera/r3.smali
@@ -1107,7 +1107,7 @@

     move-result p0

-    const-string v0, "android.provider.action.REVIEW"
+    const-string v0, "com.android.camera.action.REVIEW"

     if-eqz p0, :cond_0

@@ -1168,7 +1168,7 @@

     const-string p1, "GalleryHelper"

-    const-string v1, "gotoGallery: android.provider.action.REVIEW"
+    const-string v1, "gotoGallery: com.android.camera.action.REVIEW"

     invoke-static {p1, v1, p0}, Lcom/android/camera/log/Log;->d(Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;[Ljava/lang/Object;)V

